    "plan_id": "pilot01_sonnet55_sailor2_1b",
    "target_model": "sail/Sailor2-1B",
    "hypothesis": "Sailor2-1B is a multilingual SEA model whose Filipino and Cebuano ability is probably undertrained relative to its other languages. Small, conservative edits should be a safer bet than large ones. Mildly strengthening the value and output pathways in mid-to-late layers (v_proj, o_proj) should amplify content-carrying attention signal that already exists, which may help reading comprehension and multiple-choice answer selection. Slightly boosting the late MLP down_proj in the top layers should sharpen the final token-selection features. All edits are small positive scalings of 3-5% on a few tensors, far below the safety limits, so the model should keep its fluency. The edits are low-risk and are not expected to cause collapse. Any gain would likely be modest.",
